  "body": "Refs #45\n\nForced colors can supply a specific field background and text color. Use the\nhost's Field and FieldText pair on active and read-only text fields. Outside\nlabels and supporting text keep CanvasText. Separate actions use the Button\npair. Selected text keeps the Highlight pair.\n\nThe floating Outlined label uses the field background where it crosses the top\nedge. The field retains its layout, value, selection, and focus when the palette\nchanges. An incomplete field pair falls back to the canvas pair.\n\nThe following results used source tree 8673365398b4c7b51f5e7409abe280d79b79d852.\n\n- The workspace passed 1,595 Rust tests and three WebAssembly checks. It reported 20 ignored tests.\n- Apple Metal passed 18 offscreen tests. The archive includes 21 original PNGs.\n- The headless native Gallery used a fixed field-pair preview. Two replays produced 16 original PNGs and passed pixel readback.\n- Headless Chrome WebGPU passed 361 Material steps and 29,626 checks. It used Chrome's display emulation for light and dark cases and preserved 14 original field-pair PNGs.\n\n[Source, reproduction and local runtime evidence](https://github.com/faberline/surface/tree/2553bda78b0f55966fedeea9eb2563bac01af30a/docs/evidence/md3/text-field-system-pair-v0172-corrected-runtime)\n",
  "changed_files": 19,
